cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyunmon (동현몬): a single-player monster-collecting RPG laboratory set up through the esoteric language Donghyun-lang"
type: software
version: "0.01"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab10"
abstract: >-
  Donghyunmon is a browser-based, noncommercial monster-collecting role-playing
  game for one player. The starting town, the personality of the first
  companion, the wild-encounter rate, the starting money and the random seed are
  chosen only through programs written in the esoteric programming language
  Donghyun-lang; the adventure itself is played with the keyboard or on-screen
  buttons, using the same key layout as Donghyunjeon, Donghyunwar and
  Donghyuncr. The hero is followed by Podong-i, the author's dog; the thirteen
  creatures are borrowed from the other Donghyun laboratories. Its overall
  structure (towns and tall grass, turn-based battles, capturing with balls, a
  gym badge, a companion that follows the hero) is inspired by the Game Boy game
  Pokemon Yellow (1998); it contains none of that game's graphics, sound, maps,
  text, names or characters. Pokemon is a trademark of Nintendo, Creatures and
  Game Freak; this work is not affiliated with or endorsed by them. The MIT
  license applies to the application code, documentation and original artwork
  only; the fonts are under the SIL Open Font License, and the name and likeness
  of Podong-i remain with the author. See LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - role-playing game
  - pixel art
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
